{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>From [מאת], this [זאת]</b> — the stone that became the chief cornerstone: it was not so by its own strength, but from HaShem came this strength." "<b>And the word נפלאת</b> — from the root of 'doing wonders,' and the tav comes in place of the heh, like ושבת [and you shall return] and שכורת [intoxicated], not from wine [i.e., not from a Greek source]. And this is a sign that He speaks in the language of Israel; therefore it is marvellous in our eyes, and we shall rejoice in Him also afterward."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {1 "The phrase 'ולא מיין' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'not from wine.' The argument appears to concern the Hebrew derivation (tav replacing heh) versus some alternative, but the syntax is difficult and possibly textually corrupt. Also, 'וזה לאות כי על לשון ישראל ידבר' — the subject of 'ידבר' (He speaks) is ambiguous; rendered as referring to HaShem."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:11.376651284Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}